00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.570
And then it became a business and a hobby.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.673
- Awesome, we'll get into
that in a little bit.

00:01:11.673 --> 00:01:13.570
And you sir?

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.740
- I'm her father, Howard Greenspan.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.047
- Yes.

00:01:17.047 --> 00:01:19.933
- And I actually make slime
too, but not nearly as good.

00:01:19.933 --> 00:01:20.766
(laughing)

00:01:20.766 --> 00:01:22.450
- So let's set this up for everybody

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.660
who's listening and watching.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.660
Obviously we touched on it for a second,

00:01:28.464 --> 00:01:31.590
you know, obviously
there's also Slime Bash.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.380
And actually let's start it
that way and I'll go backwards.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.980
For everybody who's
listening, what is Slime Bash?

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.110
- So, Slime Bash is the
first ever slime convention,

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:45.410
which actually sparked a trend
of hundreds to even thousands

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:48.070
of slime conventions all over the world.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:50.000
It's basically where people can

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.110
have a booth and they can sell slime,

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.010
they can meet their internet friends,

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:57.490
trade slime and have a great time.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.783
- And how long has that been going on?

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:05.200
- Since May, around then
and then we actually...

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.819
- May of this year was the first one?

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:07.652
- Yes, May 2018.

00:02:07.652 --> 00:02:08.485
- And where was that?

00:02:08.485 --> 00:02:10.170
- That was in Stanford, Connecticut.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:11.170
- Understood.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.120
- And since then you've had how many?

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:13.953
- Two.

00:02:13.953 --> 00:02:16.090
- And the last one was in Mohegan Sun?

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:16.923
- Yes.

00:02:16.923 --> 00:02:18.740
- And there are a couple coming up?

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.600
- Yes, we have Slime
Bash Daytona, Florida,

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.840
and then we have Slime Bash Chicago.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.380
- And that's in January?

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.000
- Yes, January and March.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:28.833
- Love it.

00:02:28.833 --> 00:02:30.200
- And so you'll be
traveling to these things.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.033
- Yes.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.300
- So are you guys planning and navigating

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.760
around school schedule, what's
going on with that stuff?

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.974
- Definitely.

00:02:36.974 --> 00:02:37.807
(laughing)

00:02:37.807 --> 00:02:40.130
- So like, you have school
today, in theory, right?

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:41.154
- Yes. (laughs)

00:02:41.154 --> 00:02:44.300
- But having this podcast was
worth a missed school day?

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.210
- Definitely.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.067
- I love that.

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.760
I mean, listen for
everybody who's watching

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.860
as you can imagine I'm
aware of the slime trend,

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:52.170
my daughter got into it.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.910
But more importantly even if she hadn't,

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:57.100
I spend so much time looking
at what's popping in culture

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.470
and the internet, and no question

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:03.792
slime has been an amazing phenomenon for

00:03:03.792 --> 00:03:08.510
excuse female but plenty of
boys are into it as well,

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:12.640
excuse young but I keep watching
it get younger and older,

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.640
it's super interesting
because unlike baseball cards

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.040
which was really my version of conventions

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.683
and going to booths, and
selling and meeting people,

00:03:22.561 --> 00:03:26.060
what's amazing is people
are making the product.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.730
If you are completely lost
on this just Google around,

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.500
you'll be blown away by the capabilities

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.960
and creativity of the marketplace.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.219
So, let's take a step back.

00:03:35.219 --> 00:03:38.290
It's funny I think about,
what grade are you in?

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:39.123
- Eighth grade.

00:03:39.123 --> 00:03:44.123
- Awesome, so what in sixth
grade is when you first saw it?

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:45.093
- Yes.

00:03:45.093 --> 00:03:46.670
- And so literally as simple as,

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:49.800
and in my fifth grade year
it's funny you bring it up

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.770
when you were saying how it went down

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:53.770
it made me think of Garbage Pail Kids.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.326
There's this thing called
Garbage Pail Kids--

00:03:55.326 --> 00:03:56.159
(Maddie laughs)

00:03:56.159 --> 00:03:57.350
way back in the day, and in fifth grade

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.230
it completely took over our school.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.510
Actually I think I have
one on my wall somewhere.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.390
It completely took over out school.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:06.093
Oh yeah it's right there,
it's that little thing.

00:04:06.093 --> 00:04:06.954
That's Geeky Gary.

00:04:06.954 --> 00:04:08.420
- Yeah!

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.450
- It completely took over our school,

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.820
and it literally happened
as simple as one kid came in

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.440
the school in fifth grade that had them,

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.730
and then like complete hysteria.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.780
Were you early on the
slime trend in sixth grade?

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.250
Like your friends came in and had it,

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:27.815
and did you get on quick and
did everybody get into it?

00:04:27.815 --> 00:04:30.120
What percentage of the girls in your class

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.430
got into it, all that.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:32.263
Go.

00:04:32.263 --> 00:04:33.870
- Well, it started when my friend

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.790
brought a ton of slime to school.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.880
She pretty much filled her
entire backpack with slime

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.870
and everyone would go to her locker,

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:45.520
take some slime, and we'd just
play with it during class.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:48.020
- And your teachers let that happen?

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.634
- At first they did, now not so much.

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:51.560
- Right.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.070
- But, yeah. (laughs)

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.710
- And had you known, had you seen videos,

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.320
had you known anything about slime

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:01.030
prior to this girl
bringing slime to school.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.958
- No, I wasn't allowed
to have Instagram then.

00:05:03.958 --> 00:05:04.791
- Yep.

00:05:04.791 --> 00:05:06.210
- I didn't even know what slime was.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:07.043
- Yep.

00:05:07.043 --> 00:05:10.158
- And so, did you love it immediately?

00:05:10.158 --> 00:05:12.200
Or was it just like whatever.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.541
- I mean it was really just whatever.

00:05:14.541 --> 00:05:15.556
(Gary laughs)

00:05:15.556 --> 00:05:17.430
- I thought it was kind of
weird, I thought it was cool,

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.210
I didn't really understand
the creativity behind it

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.530
and how you can kind of make it your own.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:25.670
I thought it was just a basic
white slime and that was it.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:26.503
- Got it.

00:05:26.503 --> 00:05:29.703
And so when did it build, and
how did it build in your mind?

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:34.810
- I think in like December
of 2016 I started to make it,

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.170
I got into the trend, and
then I begged my parents

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:40.389
to let me use a slime Instagram.

00:05:40.389 --> 00:05:41.540
And then I was like...

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.540
- Were you consuming content on YouTube?

00:05:45.885 --> 00:05:47.700
- I think I was mostly Instagram then,

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.810
now it's sort of moving into YouTube.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.203
But it's mostly Instagram.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:55.220
- So how did you make your first slime?

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.191
You went to your friend's
and you were watching

00:05:57.191 --> 00:05:59.208
how-to videos, or how did it go down?

00:05:59.208 --> 00:06:00.070
- I was watching how-to videos,

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:03.900
pretty much the YouTube
slime videos were just

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:08.593
how to make basic fluffy
slime, with detergent or borax.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.480
But now it's sort of a creativity thing,

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:14.380
like slime reviews on YouTube,

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:18.850
there's slime challenges,
there's a ton of new stuff.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:23.300
- Yeah I see it, the trend
is evolving quite a bit.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:28.300
Where do you think slime is
in its cultural progression?

00:06:28.356 --> 00:06:31.920
Do you think slime's gonna
be as popular in three years?

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.740
Do you think it's gonna go up and down?

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.960
What's your gut, and I know
it's a very difficult question,

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:38.050
it's difficult for anybody,
but just your opinion

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:39.480
on where are we right now?

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:42.466
Are we at the height, do
you see it slowing down,

00:06:42.466 --> 00:06:45.066
do you see it picking up
momentum, what's your take?

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.940
- I definitely do see people
leaving the community,

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:51.347
the slime community in Instagram.

00:06:51.347 --> 00:06:53.510
Just, they're getting tired of it.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.330
But there are people who are
really evolving their business.

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.820
There's new trends like every day there's

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:01.229
a new slime trend or a new video trend.

00:07:01.229 --> 00:07:03.700
- What's the current, what's the hot thing

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.010
right now in slime?

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.330
- It's changing your containers. (laughs)

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:08.188
- [Gary] Okay.

00:07:08.188 --> 00:07:09.021
- That you put the slime in,

00:07:09.021 --> 00:07:11.500
so there's now these
like flat oval containers

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.688
rather than--

00:07:12.688 --> 00:07:13.570
- Okay, yeah.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:18.490
- Yeah but they're flat instead
of being larger and taller.

00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:19.323
- Yep.

00:07:19.323 --> 00:07:20.687
- And those are the new trend now.

00:07:20.687 --> 00:07:21.750
- That's what everybody likes?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:22.583
- Yes. (laughs)

00:07:22.583 --> 00:07:23.416
- It's bling.

00:07:23.416 --> 00:07:24.390
- The bling in the container.

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:27.317
- It's the packaging really,
is now becoming really popular.

00:07:27.317 --> 00:07:28.153
- Yeah for sure.

00:07:28.153 --> 00:07:29.320
What's your favorite
part as of this second?

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:32.100
Obviously what's so
amazingly interesting to me

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:35.965
about young entrepreneurs is
when you're in sixth grade,

00:07:35.965 --> 00:07:37.750
like when you're in eighth grade

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:40.230
your life is evolving very quickly.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.550
Not only your business, and so things

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:43.750
that you think are cool and things

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:45.980
that you're interested
in are moving very fast.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.210
And so I'm always fascinated by that.

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:51.156
For you at this point,
is it about the making,

00:07:51.156 --> 00:07:51.989
is it about the creativity,

00:07:51.989 --> 00:07:54.040
is it about building a
business with your dad?

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:58.530
What is the best part currently
of the whole slime thing?

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:02.360
- Well, I like the
creativity aspect definitely.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:05.660
I like how slime is a product

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.370
and you can make it however you'd like.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.700
It's sort of the design aspect toO,

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.410
like I can design packaging,
I can design the slime,

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:13.660
the label, everything.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.490
- Yep, so you still love making it.

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:16.323
- Yes.

00:08:16.323 --> 00:08:17.669
- That's awesome.

00:08:17.669 --> 00:08:18.502
- Thank you. (laughs)

00:08:18.502 --> 00:08:20.390
- Now jump in here and
speak to the parents

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.840
of young entrepreneurs and trends,

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:23.080
and more importantly
before we even get into

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.610
the macro of it all, I'd love to know

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:27.760
a little bit about your backstory.

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:30.350
Like you professionally,
when did this first hit you,

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:31.270
give me the whole narrative.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:33.540
What do you do, when did
it first hit your radar,

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.830
and how did things evolve
with you guys together?

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:38.778
- Okay, well I like to
think I'm an active dad.

00:08:38.778 --> 00:08:42.389
My business background is I
went to school for business,

00:08:42.389 --> 00:08:44.500
was in marketing and product development,

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.190
and I have very similar
entrepreneurial aspects.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.290
I used to sell baseball cards myself,

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:50.470
back when I was a little teen.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:51.580
- Where'd you grow up?

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:52.413
- In Connecticut.

00:08:52.413 --> 00:08:53.455
- Love it.

00:08:53.455 --> 00:08:54.288
- I used to do the shows.

00:08:54.288 --> 00:08:55.121
- Are you a New York-based sports fan

00:08:55.121 --> 00:08:56.220
or a Boston-based sports fan?

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.604
- New York based.

00:08:57.604 --> 00:08:58.437
(laughing)

00:08:58.437 --> 00:08:59.740
- Connecticut's a very weird place.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:00.573
(laughing)

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:01.607
- New York definitely.

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:02.440
- Yeah, I was definitely leading down

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:04.025
do you like the patriots
because if you do your daughter

00:09:04.025 --> 00:09:05.568
and you have to get out
of my office right now.

00:09:05.568 --> 00:09:06.401
(laughing)

00:09:06.401 --> 00:09:07.627
That's exactly where that was going.

00:09:07.627 --> 00:09:08.722
Go ahead.

00:09:08.722 --> 00:09:12.053
- Right now my company
makes a lot of products.

00:09:13.591 --> 00:09:16.270
I remember the day when Madison,

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:18.567
or Maddie, came over, sorry.

00:09:18.567 --> 00:09:19.400
(laughing)

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:20.554
When Maddie came and said--

00:09:20.554 --> 00:09:21.387
- And is Rae your middle name?

00:09:21.387 --> 00:09:22.220
- Yes.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:23.100
- Understood.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:27.310
- So Maddie came to me and
said let's go look for glue,

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:29.360
and everybody was sold out, and I'm like

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.440
I don't know what to tell you Maddie.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:33.580
And she says well can we just
make it, or can I make it.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:36.410
And that was how it all
started way back when.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:38.183
- Can I make glue?

00:09:38.183 --> 00:09:39.016
- Mm-hmm.

00:09:39.016 --> 00:09:40.295
- That's a great question.

00:09:40.295 --> 00:09:42.240
- And we're like I don't know
I've never made glue before

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.800
but I guess we can figure it out.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.615
- And it's 2019, you know.

00:09:45.615 --> 00:09:48.110
How to make glue, enter.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:50.282
- Yeah, so from a parent perspective

00:09:50.282 --> 00:09:52.856
it's wonderful working with her,

00:09:52.856 --> 00:09:54.910
doing anything with your kid because--

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:57.448
- So what happened next, I
apologize John to bring you back.

00:09:57.448 --> 00:09:58.281
- [Howard] It's all right.

00:09:58.281 --> 00:09:59.680
- So she comes, I don't know what happens

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:00.820
you found some glue somewhere

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.130
or you started trying to make glue.

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:05.371
- Well we sourced it in China. (laughs)

00:10:05.371 --> 00:10:06.204
(laughing)

00:10:06.204 --> 00:10:07.037
- You went hardcore.

00:10:07.037 --> 00:10:08.271
- Yeah.

00:10:08.271 --> 00:10:09.104
- You're like let's cut everybody out.

00:10:09.104 --> 00:10:10.620
- Well they don't really
have a glue industry

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:13.560
in the United States, so
we have to go overseas.

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.340
But you're talking about real volume.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.330
- Yeah, well--

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:17.890
- The normal person that's listening

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:19.210
they went and bought a couple Elmer's

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:21.104
and they made some slime.

00:10:21.104 --> 00:10:21.937
You know if you're going direct to China

00:10:21.937 --> 00:10:23.190
you're talking about scale.

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:25.960
- Yeah, well--

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:28.360
- How quickly did it go
from like, Maddie Rae,

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.610
from you being like I want
to make slime to like,

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:33.150
did you want to sell slime right away?

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:36.425
- I did, I didn't really know
what that really meant, so.

00:10:36.425 --> 00:10:37.258
- But you did right?

00:10:37.258 --> 00:10:38.091
I love that, by the way.

00:10:38.091 --> 00:10:39.780
That excited me.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:43.130
That is my childhood, everything
was about selling something

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:45.030
so it's just an entrepreneurial trait.

00:10:46.135 --> 00:10:51.135
- Like so many, I don't want
to mention a lot of young kids,

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:54.910
but I know 15 girls
that like making slime,

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:58.260
zero of them want to sell
it, I desperately tried.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.210
But you wanted to sell right away?

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:02.970
- I did, I didn't really
know how to make a website

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.030
or anything so it did take me a while.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:06.550
- And were you thinking that way?

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:08.590
Were you thinking make,
sell on the internet,

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:12.200
Instagram account not I'm
gonna sling this in school?

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.318
- Yes.

00:11:13.318 --> 00:11:15.570
- Did you think you'd
get some sales in school?

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:17.230
Or you didn't want to mix your business

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:18.253
with your social life?

00:11:18.253 --> 00:11:20.760
- I mean, I had friends
who were already selling it

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:21.893
at school so I didn't really think

00:11:21.893 --> 00:11:24.410
that that was a good idea to also sell.

00:11:25.721 --> 00:11:27.890
- You didn't want to get the competitive

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:29.939
business environment
to destroy friendships.

00:11:29.939 --> 00:11:30.772
- Yes. (laughing)

00:11:30.772 --> 00:11:32.722
- No, that's super smart I get it.

00:11:32.722 --> 00:11:33.722
I love that. (laughs)

00:11:33.722 --> 00:11:36.593
Okay, so what happened.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.990
When she came to you, or
when it hit your radar,

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:42.796
was it very much in the beginning

00:11:42.796 --> 00:11:45.796
or did she have interests,
you saw her making some?

00:11:45.796 --> 00:11:48.120
- I didn't really know
it was gonna be anything

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.058
to be honest.

00:11:49.058 --> 00:11:52.010
But I thought it was a good
education for her, for me.

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.049
- [Gary] Yeah you're pumped about that.

00:11:54.049 --> 00:11:57.550
- We started having board
meetings every week. (laughs)

00:11:57.550 --> 00:12:00.370
- So real quick 'cause we're
bouncing here a little bit,

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:01.857
she comes to you and
immediately it's like,

00:12:01.857 --> 00:12:03.511
"Dad I want to start a slime business."

00:12:03.511 --> 00:12:05.880
And you're like let's do this together?

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:09.330
- Well she said that, I don't make slime,

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:10.370
as I said I make a little bit now...

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:11.834
- I've heard.

00:12:11.834 --> 00:12:12.667
(Maddie laughs)

00:12:12.667 --> 00:12:13.560
- But it's not very great.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:17.010
But she wanted to talk about glue,

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:20.010
and consumer products are what I do,

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:22.020
what my company does, and I thought

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:24.710
it was a great opportunity
to do that aspect together.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:25.768
- Got it.

00:12:25.768 --> 00:12:27.620
So the thought was,
just because I'm putting

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:30.050
the pieces together,
maybe start a glue brand

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:32.800
and sell the glue because
glue was starting to dry up?

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:35.670
- Well, the idea was that, you're a parent

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:38.500
at the beginning of the glue
phase, and the slime phase,

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:41.150
and there was Elmer's and other products.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:42.810
But I remember when we first started

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:44.900
we bought rubber cement, we
didn't know what glue worked.

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:46.940
So if you have slime glue
it takes the guesswork

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:49.420
out of the parents, and
that's where it all started.

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:52.000
And now she's developed
so many different products

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.180
in the glue field, and the slime field,

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:55.013
and the accessory field.

00:12:55.013 --> 00:12:57.080
- And is that selling
on Shopify and Amazon?

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.010
Or what's happening with your products.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:01.800
- Well sell it on
SlimeMaking.com and Amazon.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:02.633
- Got it.

00:13:02.633 --> 00:13:04.640
And is that Shopify or what
are you using on the backend?

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:06.349
I'm just curious.

00:13:06.349 --> 00:13:10.292
- On the backend it's Shopify and Amazon.

00:13:10.292 --> 00:13:11.290
- Cool.

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:12.210
- Amazon uses their own interface.

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:13.220
- And who's doing the fulfillment

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:15.611
when they buy it directly
from your website?

00:13:15.611 --> 00:13:18.200
- Most things are gonna
siphon thorough Amazon.

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:19.250
- Got it, understood.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.440
And how's that experience been?

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.273
- Good.

00:13:23.273 --> 00:13:24.106
- You've learned a lot?

00:13:24.106 --> 00:13:24.939
- Yes, definitely.

00:13:24.939 --> 00:13:28.390
I learned how to run a business
which is a lot. (laughs)

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:29.223
- Do you think that's something

00:13:29.223 --> 00:13:30.647
you're gonna want to do eventually?

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:33.560
Or are you not sure yet?

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:35.510
- I don't really think I want to

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:40.290
own a business with
products but I definitely

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:43.290
would want to run my own business.

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:44.320
- Love it.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.640
So what happens next, so this starts.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:47.577
At first dad you don't
think it's gonna be that big

00:13:47.577 --> 00:13:49.660
and how quickly did you say, "Holy crap

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:50.930
there's like a whole universe of this"

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:55.050
and this is a clearly
fast-moving emerging trend

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:57.040
in society and has some legs.

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:01.350
- Well I remember we sat down,
all of us including Maddie

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:04.420
and we're just brainstorming
about fun crazy ideas

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:06.497
to get people to know about our brand.

00:14:06.497 --> 00:14:07.980
And one of the things came up,

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:09.540
why don't we break a world record.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:11.480
And Maddie's like let's
break a world record.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.130
So the team was like we can't do it.

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:16.800
And the slogan became
"We can do it." (laughs)

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:17.633
- Yeah.

00:14:17.633 --> 00:14:19.550
- So what happened there Maddie?

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:20.930
- Well, we did break the world record.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:22.690
- What was the record you went after?

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:23.960
- The world's largest slime.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:24.793
- Love it.

00:14:24.793 --> 00:14:26.053
- And what was it at the time?

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:28.954
- There wasn't actually a record

00:14:28.954 --> 00:14:30.295
so we wanted to start it.

00:14:30.295 --> 00:14:31.292
- Right, so you could've made anything.

00:14:31.292 --> 00:14:32.125
- No they tell you.

00:14:32.125 --> 00:14:32.958
- They tell you a minimum?

00:14:32.958 --> 00:14:33.791
- If there's nothing out there

00:14:33.791 --> 00:14:35.110
they're gonna make something crazy.

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:36.023
- Interesting.

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:38.310
We're talking Guinness?

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.230
- Guinness themselves.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:41.430
- That's amazing, so you held at one point

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:43.820
or still hold a Guinness
Book of World Records record?

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:44.653
- Yes.

00:14:44.653 --> 00:14:46.340
- You still hold it or somebody got crazy

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:47.260
and decided like--

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:48.780
- Oh no, no one's beat it yet. (laughs)

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:49.613
- Really?

00:14:49.613 --> 00:14:50.446
- [Maddie] Yeah.

00:14:50.446 --> 00:14:53.470
- So wait real quick,
you hold the world record

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:55.250
for the largest slime.

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:56.083
- Yes.

00:14:56.083 --> 00:14:57.310
- Which is?

00:14:57.310 --> 00:15:00.063
- 13,820 pounds.

00:15:01.046 --> 00:15:01.879
(laughing)

00:15:01.879 --> 00:15:03.027
- Where'd you put it?

00:15:03.027 --> 00:15:05.740
- Well, we put it in a giant
pool, it was really crazy.

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:08.460
We had a hundred people just in the pool

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:10.640
mixing the slime with
their hands and feet.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:11.830
- [Gary] Is that video online?

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:12.663
- [Maddie] Yes.

00:15:12.663 --> 00:15:13.590
- [Gary] Is it remarkable?

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:16.698
Like I gotta check it out,
how many views is it at?

00:15:16.698 --> 00:15:18.470
- [Howard] Oh gosh.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:20.570
- I mean we had a lot
of influencers there,

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:23.438
so every person made a different video.

00:15:23.438 --> 00:15:24.271
- Yep.

00:15:24.271 --> 00:15:26.985
- But one of our influencers
had 20 million views now.

00:15:26.985 --> 00:15:28.568
- (laughs) I love it.

00:15:28.568 --> 00:15:31.235
(Howard laughs)

00:15:33.242 --> 00:15:34.850
- There's a lot of different ones.

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:37.342
- Is it Keep Calm and Blush On?

00:15:37.342 --> 00:15:38.717
Yeah that one.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:42.162
- That's not the one.

00:15:42.162 --> 00:15:42.995
- This is it.

00:15:42.995 --> 00:15:44.670
- Yeah that's not our video, but...

00:15:46.758 --> 00:15:48.350
- Amazing.

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:51.380
- So what's the biggest thing dad

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:54.240
that you learned from this experience.

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:57.420
For obviously knowing my
audience of this podcast

00:15:57.420 --> 00:16:01.570
there's a lot of you
(laughs) listening right now,

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:03.820
what are some of your
advice, what's your tips.

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:06.500
Has there been fights,
has there been arguments?

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:09.033
How's it gone, what has made it work?

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:11.885
Keep him honest Maddie.

00:16:11.885 --> 00:16:13.028
(Maddie laughs)

00:16:13.028 --> 00:16:14.378
- I think for the most part

00:16:16.742 --> 00:16:20.060
the kids today are incredible,
they can do anything.

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:20.893
- 100%.

00:16:20.893 --> 00:16:22.220
- And I mean it's amazing.

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:25.050
Their learning capacity is
so much faster than adults.

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:25.883
- They just have so much more

00:16:25.883 --> 00:16:27.320
information at their fingertips.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:28.153
- Absolutely.

00:16:28.153 --> 00:16:29.880
- Like we could've done this too, bro.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:32.190
But the problem is we had
Beckett Baseball Card Guide

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:34.220
and that was the only information we had.

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.200
- Yeah, I learned Final Cut Pro in a month

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:38.150
and she learns it in an hour.

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:39.070
- 100%

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:40.720
- So I think it's a matter.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:42.010
- I mean you and I could've been friends,

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:43.290
I was in Jersey you were in Connecticut,

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:44.690
we could've been baseball card friends

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:47.770
but we didn't have the technology
stack called the internet

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.030
to allow us to have that.

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:52.420
- Right, people's best friends
are all over the country now.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.170
- Real quick stay on this for a second.

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:57.290
I get a lot of pushback
on modern-day parenting

00:16:57.290 --> 00:17:00.130
and technology, and everybody talks about,

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:02.590
our kids are so introverted,
they don't have social skills,

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:04.440
and I keep arguing they
have so many friends

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:06.300
in different places and are more social,

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:08.300
they're just communicating
with a different device

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:12.460
than me and you meeting at the
mall at 4:30 at the arcade.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.860
Your thoughts about that?

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:17.570
- My parents would say gosh
we're watching too much TV.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:19.860
Everything's always something
with a different age,

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:21.903
and our jobs as parents
is to understand it--

00:17:21.903 --> 00:17:23.980
- Do you know which Mike
Tyson's Punchout I played?

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:24.813
- Love it.

00:17:24.813 --> 00:17:25.646
- Unlimited.

00:17:25.646 --> 00:17:26.800
- So I get it, okay so--

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:30.629
- So our job is to
understand it and to adapt,

00:17:30.629 --> 00:17:32.490
and to encourage whatever they do.

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:34.150
- Yes culture versus no culture.

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:34.983
- Yes.

00:17:34.983 --> 00:17:36.381
- I love it.

00:17:36.381 --> 00:17:37.214
- How is the event's business?

00:17:37.214 --> 00:17:38.320
Like is this super exciting?

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.079
It seems like it's getting big.

00:17:40.079 --> 00:17:41.140
- Yes it is.

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:42.205
- Is it taxing?

00:17:42.205 --> 00:17:45.170
It's a lot of work to throw events

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:46.570
at this scale that you guys are,

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:48.200
how many people went
to the Mohegan Sun one?

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:49.517
- 7,000.

00:17:49.517 --> 00:17:51.620
- I mean you're talking
about a real business.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:52.780
- [Maddie] Yeah.

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:55.230
- How are you guys thinking
about this right now?

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:58.863
- It's an enormous undertaking.

00:18:00.114 --> 00:18:04.060
But as people I think, I'll
quote my little 6 year old,

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:06.563
and I'm sure Maddie feels the same way,

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:11.065
the greatest weekend of our life,

00:18:11.065 --> 00:18:12.340
(laughs) better than Disney World.

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:13.460
- Yeah, we asked her if she'd rather go

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:16.870
to Disney or Slime Bash and
she said Slime Bash. (laughs)

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:18.650
- Awesome, is she making slime?

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:19.757
- Yes.

00:18:19.757 --> 00:18:20.590
- I love it.

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:21.423
Is she good?

00:18:21.423 --> 00:18:22.256
She's 6 right?

00:18:22.256 --> 00:18:23.089
- Yeah.

00:18:23.089 --> 00:18:24.810
- Are you a slime snob?

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:26.120
Your reaction here is like--

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:26.998
(laughing)

00:18:26.998 --> 00:18:30.504
Do you have a high barrier to
entry to being good at slime?

00:18:30.504 --> 00:18:31.337
- Yeah.

00:18:31.337 --> 00:18:32.590
- Let's give some love to the community

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:36.890
because I'm also aware a
lot of the famous influences

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:40.810
drove to Connecticut, I'm in
the scene, I have a good sense.

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:43.280
Who do you think is doing
a good job out there

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:45.540
at making slime and promoting
themselves on YouTube,

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.290
and who did you see get a lot of love

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:48.950
at your Slime Bash at their booths.

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:51.700
Who impresses you in the community?

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:53.020
- Like the Instagrammers?

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.210
- Sure, anybody.

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:56.510
Who do you think is doing
a good job out there?

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:58.090
- I think Parakeet Slimes,

00:18:58.090 --> 00:19:00.100
she's a great influence on people.

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:01.743
She had a huge line.

00:19:01.743 --> 00:19:02.576
- [Gary] Yep, I saw.

00:19:02.576 --> 00:19:04.040
- People really love her account,

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:05.733
they love her personality.

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:07.543
- Who else?

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:12.460
- Karina Garcia, she has
8 million subscribers.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.893
It was really great to
see her meeting everyone.

00:19:16.276 --> 00:19:18.040
- Yep, she's pretty OG right,

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:20.010
like she's like a big name.

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:23.060
- Yeah, she was definitely one
of the first slime accounts,

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:24.673
she's also DIY too.

00:19:27.367 --> 00:19:31.330
And then also I think
everyone in Slimers Alley

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.350
which is sort of like the rising slimers.

00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:36.250
They all gained so many
followers from Slime Bash,

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:38.840
it was really great to see that too.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.390
- What are your friends
thinking about this?

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:42.143
Now in eighth grade versus sixth grade.

00:19:42.143 --> 00:19:46.240
It's very, just knowing kids,
it's really interesting.

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:49.470
You're starting to go to another
chapter of your adolescence

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:53.810
and do they think slime's not as cool

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:56.037
but it's cool that you're in business?

00:19:56.037 --> 00:19:58.463
What's the take right now?

00:19:59.991 --> 00:20:03.297
Are you in a school where
eighth grade is the oldest grade

00:20:03.297 --> 00:20:04.610
and there's younger kids in the school?

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:05.960
- [Maddie] Yes.

00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:08.470
- So do some of the fourth
graders think you're famous

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:09.490
and want to take selfies?

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:11.750
- What's happening in
the trenches at school?

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:14.230
- Well, the little kids
it's really funny they

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:15.720
always like come up to me--

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:17.240
- Are you K through eight, or
are you fifth through eight?

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:20.110
- We're Pre-K, three, four,
and then K through eight.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.640
- Right, so that's interesting.

00:20:21.640 --> 00:20:22.473
Go ahead.

00:20:22.473 --> 00:20:24.120
So what's happening with the youngsters?

00:20:25.463 --> 00:20:27.650
- They're not really on Instagram,

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:29.620
but one time I did receive
a really sweet note

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.750
from a little fourth grader who asked

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.368
if I wanted to hang out with her one day

00:20:34.368 --> 00:20:36.268
and make slime, which was really nice.

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:39.603
But a lot of my friends at
school they don't like slime,

00:20:39.603 --> 00:20:43.140
some of them really hate it but they think

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:44.400
Slime Bash is really cool,

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:46.570
they all went to the world record.

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:48.366
So, yeah.

00:20:48.366 --> 00:20:49.781
- That's how it's working.

00:20:49.781 --> 00:20:52.040
You know, one of the things
that's really interesting to me

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:55.640
about this trend and you just
brought it up with Garcia,

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:57.480
I'd like to get your thoughts on this.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.850
The do it yourself movement,
do you think that slime

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:03.730
is going to graduate a lot of young girls

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:07.350
into being creators in other areas?

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:10.780
- Definitely, I think a
lot of people are actually

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:13.913
moving to vlogging, like Parakeet Slimes

00:21:13.913 --> 00:21:16.045
who I was talking about before,

00:21:16.045 --> 00:21:20.283
she's now doing school vlogs all the time.

00:21:22.294 --> 00:21:24.010
- What about soap?

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:24.900
Have you seen that?

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:26.671
- Oh yeah, soap cutting. (laughs)

00:21:26.671 --> 00:21:28.482
- Yeah what are you seeing with that?

00:21:28.482 --> 00:21:31.920
- ASMR in general,
(laughs) like eating ASMR.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:33.693
- Of course.

00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:37.603
- Yeah there's eating
ASMR, there's slime ASMR,

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:41.240
like ASMR is kind of a large category now

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:43.963
so people are definitely
moving towards that too.

00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:49.210
- What else should
parents know about this,

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:51.250
think about it, entrepreneurship, slime,

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:53.620
what's some of your hot takes?

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:56.400
- Well, I think the key is that

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:58.120
there's always gonna be something,

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:01.780
and parents you don't always
have to approve of anything.

00:22:01.780 --> 00:22:04.050
Most parents are beginning
it in their households

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:06.446
because of the mess, and kids make messes.

00:22:06.446 --> 00:22:09.947
I think it's better to
teach them responsibleness

00:22:09.947 --> 00:22:13.090
of making slime, make them
clean up after themselves.

00:22:13.090 --> 00:22:14.010
- Yeah its a mess.

00:22:14.010 --> 00:22:15.700
- But if you make them clean up

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:18.000
versus just saying gee
it's going to be a mess

00:22:18.851 --> 00:22:20.250
I think you have to temper what you do

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:21.660
to what you encourage your kids

00:22:21.660 --> 00:22:23.760
versus what you don't encourage your kids.

00:22:24.644 --> 00:22:26.590
Because there's a domino effect positively

00:22:26.590 --> 00:22:29.090
and negative to whatever
you do to your kids.

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:30.330
- I couldn't agree more.

00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:32.780
Talk to me about, you
talked about marketing

00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:34.830
and being an entrepreneur,
what have you learned

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:36.880
about the current state of marketing

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:40.583
through this adventure
of slime, if anything.

00:22:42.430 --> 00:22:45.240
- Well, I've learned a lot
about the influencer world

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:50.240
which is not my bandwagon,
that's the new generation,

00:22:52.370 --> 00:22:54.800
the power of the
generation, this generation

00:22:54.800 --> 00:22:59.523
could move the NFL to shut
down just with a couple tweets.

00:23:00.514 --> 00:23:04.260
So it's really fascinating
that just in a niche

00:23:04.260 --> 00:23:07.660
of something to the new, let me go back,

00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:12.660
the new superstars are Parakeet
Slimes versus Taylor Swift.

00:23:13.340 --> 00:23:16.420
I think if they were both next
to each other at Slime Bash,

00:23:16.420 --> 00:23:18.420
I think Parakeet would have a larger line.

00:23:18.420 --> 00:23:19.253
- [Gary] I understand.

00:23:19.253 --> 00:23:20.470
- And that's fascinating, and I think

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:22.497
we all have to understand it because this

00:23:22.497 --> 00:23:24.330
is the generation that's
gonna rule the next world.

00:23:24.330 --> 00:23:25.580
- 100%.

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:27.080
Any questions you have for me?

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:32.511
- Are you sure you want
to buy the Jets? (laughs)

00:23:32.511 --> 00:23:33.786
- 100,000%.

00:23:33.786 --> 00:23:34.619
(laughing)

00:23:34.619 --> 00:23:36.680
More than anything professionally.

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:37.513
- Can you make them good?

00:23:37.513 --> 00:23:41.640
- 100,000%, because everything
in life stems from the top.

00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:42.620
- Then I'm not gonna buy it,

00:23:42.620 --> 00:23:44.645
I'm gonna go for the Tampa Bay Buccaneers,

00:23:44.645 --> 00:23:45.478
I'll let you have that.

00:23:45.478 --> 00:23:46.311
(laughing)

00:23:46.311 --> 00:23:47.863
- Is Tampa on your radar, or just random?

00:23:50.140 --> 00:23:53.220
Maddie what should, for
everybody who's listening,

00:23:53.220 --> 00:23:55.840
what should they know
about the slime movement,

00:23:55.840 --> 00:23:58.523
the DIY movement, just the whole scene.

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:03.150
- I think that a lot of people
view slime as like a fad,

00:24:03.150 --> 00:24:06.444
or in a trend but really
there's a large community

00:24:06.444 --> 00:24:09.500
of people who are making
it and it's now a job

00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:13.161
for a ton of people, so yeah. (laughs)

00:24:13.161 --> 00:24:15.027
- What's been the most surprising thing

00:24:15.027 --> 00:24:18.550
in the last month, in the trends, sales

00:24:19.410 --> 00:24:22.390
anything stand out to
you if I'm just trying to

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:23.710
siphon some IP from you

00:24:23.710 --> 00:24:26.100
on things that are
happening in the trenches.

00:24:26.100 --> 00:24:27.600
What's kind of interesting?

00:24:27.600 --> 00:24:30.940
So I like the flat
container thing, what else?

00:24:30.940 --> 00:24:35.120
- Well now slime acrobatics
are actually becoming a thing.

00:24:35.120 --> 00:24:37.360
So there's something
called slime flipping,

00:24:37.360 --> 00:24:39.420
where you take the slime
and you flip it and--

00:24:39.420 --> 00:24:42.414
- Try to make a big like bubble?

00:24:42.414 --> 00:24:45.310
- It's not really making
a bubble it's like

00:24:45.310 --> 00:24:46.790
doing tricks with the slime.

00:24:46.790 --> 00:24:48.904
- Yep, so that's the acrobatics?

00:24:48.904 --> 00:24:50.501
- So, yeah, it's like the way you flip it.

00:24:50.501 --> 00:24:51.467
- Are you doing that?

00:24:51.467 --> 00:24:54.030
- I'm really bad at it, so not really,

00:24:54.030 --> 00:24:57.330
but there are people who
have made really cool videos

00:24:57.330 --> 00:25:00.380
of them flipping slime,
so it's really cool

00:25:00.380 --> 00:25:02.680
to see the new tricks
that people come up with.

00:25:02.680 --> 00:25:04.375
- I love it, so, please.

00:25:04.375 --> 00:25:07.010
- I had a question though,
I'd love to know your thoughts

00:25:07.010 --> 00:25:10.250
just in general about the conventions,

00:25:10.250 --> 00:25:13.823
because one of the things
that we find fascinating,

00:25:13.823 --> 00:25:17.640
or I do, is that this is
one of the first times

00:25:17.640 --> 00:25:21.322
that you have this internet
world of influencers

00:25:21.322 --> 00:25:23.760
and millions of kids around the world

00:25:23.760 --> 00:25:24.870
that are actually leaving the internet

00:25:24.870 --> 00:25:27.150
and coming to meet their communities,

00:25:27.150 --> 00:25:29.190
and inspiring kids to come out.

00:25:29.190 --> 00:25:31.190
- This is happening and has been happening

00:25:31.190 --> 00:25:33.810
for the last half decade, the trend of

00:25:33.810 --> 00:25:35.537
as we live in a digital world

00:25:35.537 --> 00:25:38.510
it enhances real-life experiences.

00:25:38.510 --> 00:25:42.186
Whether it's as simple as
people going and taking a hike

00:25:42.186 --> 00:25:45.310
because they want the
photo for their Instagram.

00:25:45.310 --> 00:25:48.940
Or look, when Vine was popping a lot of

00:25:48.940 --> 00:25:51.890
the teeny bopper boys, Nash
Greer and Cameron Dallas,

00:25:51.890 --> 00:25:53.470
and these characters they went on tour

00:25:53.470 --> 00:25:56.941
and had 30,000, 40,000, VidCon
gets hundreds of thousands.

00:25:56.941 --> 00:26:00.687
This has been going on and
will continue to go on.

00:26:00.687 --> 00:26:02.567
I do think that there will be,

00:26:02.567 --> 00:26:05.550
whether it's fads or
long trends like look,

00:26:05.550 --> 00:26:07.280
when your dad and I were growing up

00:26:07.280 --> 00:26:10.250
baseball cards were massive,
then for 20 years they weren't,

00:26:10.250 --> 00:26:11.800
now there's a bubbling up again.

00:26:11.800 --> 00:26:14.840
Like to your point I
don't think slime will be

00:26:14.840 --> 00:26:19.225
as white hot as it is
right now in perpetuity.

00:26:19.225 --> 00:26:21.840
It will peak and valley,
but do I think it got

00:26:21.840 --> 00:26:26.500
so hot and so at scale that
it will now have cycles, I do.

00:26:26.500 --> 00:26:29.020
I feel like if I was predicting

00:26:29.020 --> 00:26:31.070
I'd be like okay it has another
three years of goodness.

00:26:31.070 --> 00:26:32.780
Then it starts really
kind of calming down.

00:26:32.780 --> 00:26:35.350
It's still happening, there's
still plenty of people making,

00:26:35.350 --> 00:26:38.420
but it's not in the zeitgeist,
attendance to something

00:26:38.420 --> 00:26:40.820
like Slime Bash peaks at 50,000,

00:26:40.820 --> 00:26:43.970
goes down to 8,000 and
6,000 seven years later

00:26:43.970 --> 00:26:46.398
if you guys ran it forever,
and then it reboots.

00:26:46.398 --> 00:26:47.870
That's what always happens, that's what

00:26:47.870 --> 00:26:49.930
happens with G.I. Joe, that's
what happens with wrestling.

00:26:49.930 --> 00:26:52.640
That's what happens with '90s clothes,

00:26:52.640 --> 00:26:55.000
that's what happening now
with Fila and Tommy Hilfiger.

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:57.720
So what I think Slime has accomplished

00:26:57.720 --> 00:27:00.840
that a lot of other fads don't,

00:27:00.840 --> 00:27:03.230
where they only have a six month window,

00:27:03.230 --> 00:27:05.770
and nine month white heat window,

00:27:05.770 --> 00:27:07.820
pencil fighting, do you
remember pencil fighting?

00:27:07.820 --> 00:27:08.810
Did you have that?

00:27:08.810 --> 00:27:10.484
- [Howard] Whenever they flick 'em?

00:27:10.484 --> 00:27:11.317
- Yeah.

00:27:11.317 --> 00:27:12.150
- [Howard] Yeah.

00:27:12.150 --> 00:27:14.220
- So that was huge for us
in sixth and seventh grade.

00:27:14.220 --> 00:27:17.312
That wasn't big enough, and
didn't sustain long enough

00:27:17.312 --> 00:27:20.800
that it's coming back every
five, seven, ten years,

00:27:20.800 --> 00:27:22.550
I do think slime has that.

00:27:22.550 --> 00:27:25.960
As far as the events, marketing business,

00:27:25.960 --> 00:27:27.650
I couldn't be more bullish.

00:27:27.650 --> 00:27:28.690
I couldn't be more bullish.

00:27:28.690 --> 00:27:31.018
I think what you put in the container

00:27:31.018 --> 00:27:35.200
of these convention centers
and casinos will change.

00:27:35.200 --> 00:27:37.310
Some things have 100-year runs,

00:27:37.310 --> 00:27:40.100
some things have 3-year
blips then they come back.

00:27:40.100 --> 00:27:43.418
But yeah I think of it like Aerosmith

00:27:43.418 --> 00:27:46.553
and Rolling Stones and Run DMC.

00:27:46.553 --> 00:27:49.350
Once you can establish
something it ebbs and flows,

00:27:49.350 --> 00:27:51.033
but it's always kind of around.

00:27:51.900 --> 00:27:53.030
- [Howard] Absolutely.

00:27:53.030 --> 00:27:57.037
- Look it's an intense
business, it's taxing right.

00:27:57.037 --> 00:28:00.030
You could make a lot of,
you could build a warehouse

00:28:00.030 --> 00:28:01.580
in your back yard if you had the space

00:28:01.580 --> 00:28:04.320
to make a ton of slime, and sell it

00:28:04.320 --> 00:28:07.730
through Amazon, but schlepping to Daytona

00:28:07.730 --> 00:28:09.292
and making sure everything's right.

00:28:09.292 --> 00:28:11.758
But the experience is like look,

00:28:11.758 --> 00:28:14.980
I'm in agreement with your 6 year old,

00:28:14.980 --> 00:28:18.610
the thought that your family's
gonna have this adventure

00:28:18.610 --> 00:28:20.474
and remember this time
together too is just

00:28:20.474 --> 00:28:23.050
disproportionately valuable in my opinion.

00:28:23.050 --> 00:28:25.040
- Absolutely, and we do it
all together so it's great.

00:28:25.040 --> 00:28:26.140
- Oh I have a question for you Maddie,

00:28:26.140 --> 00:28:28.190
one thing that I'm very passionate about

00:28:28.190 --> 00:28:32.560
is what I call the super
premium category of any product.

00:28:32.560 --> 00:28:34.910
I'm always most interested in how much

00:28:34.910 --> 00:28:37.140
can you actually charge
for something, right.

00:28:37.140 --> 00:28:39.130
So for example a big dream of mine

00:28:39.130 --> 00:28:42.040
has always been to start
a $20 pack of bubble gum.

00:28:42.040 --> 00:28:43.970
Like that's expensive for bubble gum.

00:28:43.970 --> 00:28:47.530
But $20 is achievable for a lot of people,

00:28:47.530 --> 00:28:49.490
so I've always thought it's
an interesting category.

00:28:49.490 --> 00:28:52.900
What's the most expensive
slime you've seen?

00:28:52.900 --> 00:28:56.250
What was the single most
expensive slime sold at Slime Bash

00:28:56.250 --> 00:28:58.870
or you've seen recently on
Instagram from an influencer?

00:28:58.870 --> 00:29:01.303
Has anybody made something
really expensive yet?

00:29:02.580 --> 00:29:05.310
- Well there's 32 ounces are becoming

00:29:05.310 --> 00:29:06.860
a really big trend now.

00:29:06.860 --> 00:29:09.123
- And what were the ounces before that?

00:29:10.921 --> 00:29:15.297
- Most people sell in
2, 4, 6, and 8 ounces.

00:29:15.297 --> 00:29:16.379
So 32 ounces--

00:29:16.379 --> 00:29:17.212
- 32 is like bulk.

00:29:17.212 --> 00:29:18.123
- Yeah it's really big.

00:29:19.045 --> 00:29:22.740
I've seen people charge
as much as $50 for them.

00:29:22.740 --> 00:29:25.740
- What's the most expensive 8 ounce slime

00:29:25.740 --> 00:29:27.559
you can think of that you've seen

00:29:27.559 --> 00:29:29.470
in the last year and a half?

00:29:29.470 --> 00:29:31.490
- Probably $17.

00:29:31.490 --> 00:29:32.840
- [Gary] And what was that?

00:29:34.200 --> 00:29:36.770
- I believe it was a butter
slime because it contained

00:29:36.770 --> 00:29:40.080
a lot of daiso clay
which is very expensive.

00:29:40.080 --> 00:29:40.913
- Understood.

00:29:40.913 --> 00:29:42.290
- And scent, so fragrance oil.

00:29:42.290 --> 00:29:44.930
- Yeah the scent thing seems
to be popping too, right?

00:29:44.930 --> 00:29:46.890
- Yeah, it's very expensive though.

00:29:46.890 --> 00:29:50.580
So a 32 ounce would use a bottle of scent.

00:29:50.580 --> 00:29:51.413
- Understood.

00:29:51.413 --> 00:29:52.500
- But you bring an interesting point,

00:29:52.500 --> 00:29:56.300
I wonder if there's like, you
could put real gold flakes

00:29:56.300 --> 00:29:58.800
in something or limited
edition of only seven made.

00:29:58.800 --> 00:29:59.920
- Yeah I mean when you get big enough,

00:29:59.920 --> 00:30:01.670
when you're Parakeet,
when you're Brian Anthony,

00:30:01.670 --> 00:30:04.120
like these kind of
characters you could just say

00:30:04.120 --> 00:30:07.683
I'm only making 25 of these,
here's what I'm doing with it.

00:30:08.910 --> 00:30:12.040
I do think, look again I'm using it 'cause

00:30:12.040 --> 00:30:15.277
it's our context point,
Upper Deck came along.

00:30:15.277 --> 00:30:16.677
- Yep, where they had limited runs.

00:30:16.677 --> 00:30:18.390
- Yep, just it was expensive.

00:30:18.390 --> 00:30:19.940
We were paying 50 cents a pack for cards

00:30:19.940 --> 00:30:21.319
and then it was $2, it was like

00:30:21.319 --> 00:30:23.490
(imitating explosion
sound) that was insanity.

00:30:23.490 --> 00:30:25.990
I do think there's an absolute category

00:30:25.990 --> 00:30:29.140
for one of the influencers
to take that leap

00:30:29.140 --> 00:30:31.370
and create a super premium category.

00:30:31.370 --> 00:30:34.350
And I do think that there
are plenty of people,

00:30:34.350 --> 00:30:36.370
like Maddie this may
sound interesting to you

00:30:36.370 --> 00:30:38.050
given that you're in the trenches,

00:30:38.050 --> 00:30:42.340
I do believe that there
is a $50 8 ounce slime

00:30:42.340 --> 00:30:44.533
to be sold in the slime
community, I really do.

00:30:44.533 --> 00:30:46.270
- There's the advent calendar.

00:30:46.270 --> 00:30:51.110
- Yeah some people, I've
seen someone charge $169

00:30:51.110 --> 00:30:52.440
for an advent calendar.

00:30:52.440 --> 00:30:53.840
- What's an advent calendar?

00:30:56.761 --> 00:30:57.911
- You've confused Gary.

00:30:59.119 --> 00:31:00.270
(inaudible)

00:31:00.270 --> 00:31:02.250
- Oh that's the open thing?

00:31:02.250 --> 00:31:03.450
That's what it's called?

00:31:04.590 --> 00:31:06.310
- 25 days of slime.

00:31:06.310 --> 00:31:07.143
- [Gary] That's awesome.

00:31:07.143 --> 00:31:08.870
- It's not really like a door,
you don't open the doors.

00:31:08.870 --> 00:31:11.800
It's just a giant box full of 25 slimes.

00:31:11.800 --> 00:31:12.730
- Understood.

00:31:12.730 --> 00:31:14.373
25 slimes for a buck what?

00:31:15.717 --> 00:31:17.240
- $169.

00:31:17.240 --> 00:31:18.200
- What for 25 slimes?

00:31:18.200 --> 00:31:19.407
- Yeah so that's pretty good.

00:31:19.407 --> 00:31:20.930
- I mean that's a good deal,

00:31:20.930 --> 00:31:21.990
but I understand the bulk of it.

00:31:21.990 --> 00:31:24.400
No really I'm really curious if somebody's

00:31:24.400 --> 00:31:27.990
gonna come out and make
$49 slime in an 8 ounce

00:31:27.990 --> 00:31:31.274
and say that the tears
of a seal are a part,

00:31:31.274 --> 00:31:32.887
really like that's the stuff.

00:31:32.887 --> 00:31:34.950
Or one could, you know listen

00:31:34.950 --> 00:31:38.653
what's amazing about the
internet is there some,

00:31:38.653 --> 00:31:41.470
can you add the water from
a creek in your backyard

00:31:41.470 --> 00:31:43.010
and because you've been
vlogging and everybody

00:31:43.010 --> 00:31:45.350
gives a crap about that
creek, like there's so much

00:31:45.350 --> 00:31:48.983
creativity that is still yet to be solved.

00:31:51.770 --> 00:31:54.270
- For the conventions
there's the mega bash ticket

00:31:54.270 --> 00:31:56.250
which gives people a premium,

